---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const BASE = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Contact"
  description="Email, Cal.com, social. No spam form."
  lede="No web form. The fastest path is email. Brief, specific, with the deadline if there is one."
  nav="contact"
>
  <section class="cta-grid">
    <a class="cta" href="mailto:hello@felixgeelhaar.com">
      <h3>Email</h3>
      <p>hello@felixgeelhaar.com — I reply within a week.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="cta" href="https://cal.com/felixgeelhaar">
      <h3>Book a call</h3>
      <p>30 minutes to decide whether an engagement fits.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="cta" href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar">
      <h3>GitHub</h3>
      <p>Issues on the OSS projects get the fastest answer there.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="cta" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/felixgeelhaar/">
      <h3>LinkedIn</h3>
      <p>For inbound that needs a paper trail.</p>
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Before you write</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>One paragraph. What is happening, what you have tried, what you want to be true in 90 days.</li>
      <li>Names. Specific. "Acme Corp" beats "a Series B SaaS company".</li>
      <li>Deadline if there is one. "By end of quarter" beats "soon".</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Speaker invitations: include the topic, the audience, the date, and the previous year's recording
      if it exists. Sponsorship and press: <a href={`${BASE}about`}>see About</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
